<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Corsica</h1><p class="st-meta">1736 CE – 1736 CE · capital Cervione</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The eight-month kingdom of Theodore von Neuhoff, a German adventurer crowned by Corsican rebels against Genoa in 1736.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Corsicans had been in revolt against Genoese rule since 1729. In March 1736 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodore-von-neuhoff">Theodore von Neuhoff</a>, a Westphalian baron, landed with arms and money from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a>, and in April the rebel leaders crowned him king at the convent of Alesani, with a constitution limiting his power.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Theodore set up a court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cervione">Cervione</a>, created orders of knighthood, minted coins and issued titles, but failed to take the Genoese-held coastal towns. Promised foreign aid did not arrive, and his support among the rebel chiefs waned.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In November 1736 Theodore left <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/corsican-republic">Corsica</a> to seek help. His later attempts to return failed, and he ended in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> debtors' prison, dying in 1756. The revolt continued and later produced the Corsican Republic.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-corsica.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Corsica" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: Jimmy44 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Corsica_(before_1755).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1736 CE – 1736 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cervione</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Theodore of Corsica</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Corsican and Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Corsica (1736)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1736&amp;focus=kingdom-of-corsica" aria-label="Kingdom of Corsica on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4902 677 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Corsica lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5222 933L5214 863"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5214 863h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5222 933h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5222 933h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1736&amp;focus=kingdom-of-corsica">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
